# Do Not Touch: Protected Core Files

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` is the dispatch/subscribe engine and `app/src/types.ts`
defines the `Action` union, `AppState`, and domain types. These files are the
contract everything else depends on. Accidental changes ripple across the whole
app and break existing tests.

## Rule

- DO NOT modify `app/src/store.ts` without explicit user approval.
- DO NOT modify `app/src/types.ts` without explicit user approval.
- If a task requires changes to these files, ASK the user first and explain
  what change is needed and why.
- Adding new action variants to `types.ts` is the most common legitimate
  edit — even then, confirm before writing.

## How to verify

1. `git diff --name-only` — `app/src/store.ts` and `app/src/types.ts` should NOT appear unless the user explicitly approved the change.
2. Check conversation history for explicit approval before any edit to these files.
